# EMS .gitignore
#
# Deliberately hand-written. `dotnet new gitignore` emits ~490 lines covering
# tooling this project does not use, and among them `docs/` and `tests/`, which
# would silently exclude the specification, the ADRs, and all three test
# projects from every commit.
#
# These must stay committed and are called out here so nobody adds them:
#   packages.lock.json  - reproducible restore depends on it
#   tests/              - first-class source, not build output
#
# docs/ was committed until 2026-08-19 and is now deliberately excluded. It stays
# on disk and stays normative for anyone working in this checkout; it simply does
# not travel with the repository.

# Build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
artifacts/

# Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.rsuser
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.userprefs

# Secrets and local configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
appsettings.*.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# SQL Server database files
*.mdf
*.ldf

# Test, coverage, and Playwright output
[Tt]est[Rr]esults/
test-results/
coverage-report/
*.trx
*.coverage
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/
playwright-traces/

# MSBuild diagnostics
*.binlog

# Local run/launch scratch output
*.log

# NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code configuration, hooks and local permissions
.claude/

# Specification, architecture, implementation guide and ADRs. Local only.
docs/

# Analyzer ban list. Directory.Build.props generates it into obj/ on every build,
# so nothing at the repository root should carry this name. Ignored as a guard
# against the tracked root file coming back. See ADR-0014.
BannedSymbols.txt
